        "exact_choice_count": null,
        "notes": "Scheduled intakes September each year. Application processing Ongoing throughout the year. Recommended for success This program is specifically designed for individuals either seeking a career in the water or wastewater sector or for those currently employed in the water and wastewater industry, but have not received formal training. To be successful in this program, students are recommended to have the following: English language proficiency: Category 2 \u2013 English Studies 12 (67%) or equivalent Math: one of the following: Pre-Calculus 11 (67%) or Foundations of Math 11 (67%) or Workplace Math 11 (67%) or Other acceptable BC and Yukon courses Chemistry 11 (67%) High school graduation (or equivalent) is an EOCP requirement for certification. If you do not meet the above entry recommendations, you can consult with the program administration to discuss your particular situation. International applicants This program is not available to international students. View available programs . Apply to program Applications for this program are processed by the SOCE Industry Services department. Please contact Andrea Dusanj for more information or to receive a registration package. Go back Overview Next up Costs & Supplies",
